# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) for local development.
# In production these are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`.

# A tablet signs in by redeeming a claim link. Mint the first one against the
# seeded device:
#   npm run claim:bootstrap -w @pos/api -- dev_counter --local

# HMAC key for identity tokens, and the key the staff PIN hashes are keyed
# with. Changing it signs every tablet out and makes every stored PIN stop
# matching, so pick one per environment and leave it alone. Generate a real one
# for production:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
AUTH_SECRET=dev-only-secret-do-not-use-in-production

# Optional. Without these, realtime is disabled and the cashier page polls
# every 5s instead — which is a perfectly usable way to develop, and means
# local dev needs no Upstash account and no cloud resources at all.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://xxx.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=xxx
